21: 2.1.1 Structure of Prompts for Generative AI in Software testing
      Why structure of prompts is important in GenAI
      > Gen AI ouputs depend heavily on how prompts are designed
      > A well - structure prompt ensures accuracy, relevance and quality in testware generation
      > A structured promopt for sotware testing typically includes six components
          
RCIICO
          > Role
          > Context 
          > Intruction
          > Input Data
          > Contraints
          > Output format

      > Prompts are like blueprint for GenAI which guides the AI's response

    > ROLE : 
        > Defines the perspective or persona that the GenAI model should take when generating a response (eg. tester, test manager, automation engineer)
        > Shapes tome and responsibility
        Ex: Act as a functional tester and design functional test testcases

    > CONTEXT :
        > Provides the background information that the GenAI model nees to determine the test conditions (test object, functionallity, environment)
        Ex: We are testing the login module of a banking app

    > INSTRUCTION :
        > Clear, concise directives for the task
        Ex: Generate boundary test cases for username length betweeen 5 to 15 characters

    > INPUT DATA :
        > Includes user stories, acceptance criteria, screenshots, code or existing test cases
        > It helps GenAI to generate context-aware results
        Ex: Provding acceptance criteria : "System must lock account after 3 failed login attempts

    > CONSTRAINTS :
        > Define restrictions or special considerations
        Ex: Generate test cases only for functional testing, exclude performance scenarios

    > OUTPUT FORMAT :
        > Specifies expected structure or style of response
        Ex: Provide test cases in Gherkin format (Give - When - Then)


